# paper/ holds the 1913 scan (~19.5 MB, library digitisation of unstated terms)
# and Antonio Ciccone's 2023 English translation, which is a copyrighted modern
# scholarly work. Neither is ours to redistribute.
# What the historical limb actually rests on is shipped instead: the double-entry
# transcription in data/derived/auerbach-1913-*.csv and the discrepancy record in
# results/stage1-transcription-diff.md.
paper/

# Metron 7(2) (1928) is a whole third-party journal issue mirrored from ISTAT's
# digital library, containing other authors' articles alongside Saibante's. Only
# the transcribed 17-country table is redistributed. Source URL, byte size and
# SHA-256 are recorded in data/CONTRACT.md, Addendum 1.
data/raw/saibante-1928/

# Scaruffi's compiled highest-mountains list, captured 2026-09-03 because the
# archive.org availability API reports zero snapshots of it and it is the source of
# Miskinis's 548-summit set. Preservation only: a third-party copyrighted
# compilation we have no licence to redistribute, and it is not parsed, fitted, or
# referenced by any result. Full status in the _manifest.json there.
data/raw/scaruffi-2026-09-03/

